id: pm-ado-lmey
title: Install the pinned release npm into a job-local prefix
description: "The release workflow replaces the runner's global npm with the pinned npm. Parallel jobs on one runner host share the toolcache Node installation, so one job's global install mutates a sibling job's npm mid-install (ENOTEMPTY, or npm: command not found), as reported by unbraind/pm-ops#284 for the fleet."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: "gh:unbraind/pm-ado#116","gh:unbraind/pm-ops#284"
created_at: "2026-11-16T14:41:52.475Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-17T08:29:07.433Z"
author: pi-glm
acceptance_criteria: The release workflow installs the pinned npm with --prefix into a job-local directory and prepends that prefix bin to the job path; The workflow keeps the exact-version assertion on the effective npm; A workflow-contract test fails if any workflow replaces the global npm
comments[19]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-16T15:17:20.034Z",codex-sol,"Continuation: verified the existing worktree and remote branch state, preserved the earlier changes, and reused this item. Rerunning required gates to completion under the continuation author before committing results."
  "2026-11-16T15:27:41.370Z",codex-sol,"Root cause confirmed in the workflow source: global installation of the pinned npm replaces the same Node installation used by parallel jobs on a shared toolcache. Replaced each bootstrap with a job-local prefix, published only its bin directory to the job PATH, and retained exact-pin checks including a separate subsequent-step assertion. Workflow contracts reject global npm replacement across all workflow files. No runner settings or shared tool installations were modified."
  "2026-11-16T15:32:08.555Z",codex-sol,"Validation note: this package defines no lint script. Its existing docstring static gate is being run with typecheck, the quick npm test tier, the release workflow contracts and changelog:check; no new lint policy or dependency is introduced for this CI fix."
  "2026-11-16T15:42:12.914Z",codex-sol,The first combined gate command hit its 20-minute timeout during shared-host disk contention and is not pass evidence. Retrying all gates to completion using memory-backed temporary fixtures and the existing harness deadline scale. Assertions and test selection are unchanged.
  "2026-11-16T15:50:16.961Z",codex-sol,"The provenance failures observed during the disk-contention attempt were rechecked separately without source changes: node --test test/closeout-provenance.test.ts completed with all 8 tests passed, no skips or cancellations, using memory-backed temporary fixtures. The complete package gate rerun remains separate evidence."
  "2026-11-16T16:07:40.748Z",codex-sol,"Typecheck and the existing docstring static gate passed; this package has no lint script. Focused workflow tests passed 19 of 20, with the unrelated nested preload acceptance timing out under disk contention. The separate provenance recheck passed all 8 tests. Broad quick gates are active; the preload case will be rechecked from an isolated temporary checkout."
  "2026-11-16T16:20:00.016Z",codex-sol,"Implementation commit 3906f079bba749ff3c71774c24d83514a349f8da is verified by all 20 workflow-contract tests, including the nested preload acceptance, run to completion from an isolated temporary checkout of that exact commit. The separate changelog:check passed; typecheck and the existing docstring gate passed. This package has no lint script. The initial focused preload timeout is superseded by the completed contract rerun. Broad quick tests remain active, and remote CI is pending the shared runner hold. Releasing the claim for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-16T16:47:56.999Z",codex-sol,"The broad local retry reached its 60-minute command limit: 604 tests reported 601 passed, 2 failed and 1 cancelled. Remaining failures concern packed consumer acceptance and the nested preload run; that complete 20-test workflow suite separately passed from the isolated committed checkout, and changelog:check passed. The broad suite is not certified green. Tracking PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ado/pull/116. The PR remains open for orchestrator verification; exact-head CI is queued or running."
  "2026-11-16T19:23:52.314Z",codex-sol,"Review round P: replace the workflow-wide regex with a dependency-free shell command parser and regression fixtures. Parse run scripts with existing yaml where available; preserve allowed prefix-local installs. Verify typecheck, lint or docstring, focused guard/workflow contracts and changelog checks before pushing. No review-thread actions."
  "2026-11-16T19:28:59.317Z",codex-sol,"Review round P addresses PRRT_kwDOUMUq1864FZHh: replace the regex with the same dependency-free command parser as pm-ops, using the permitted raw-text workflow scan because no yaml parser is declared here. The scan joins shell continuations and unwraps simple quoted run scalars. Added 38 fixtures covering aliases, flags, locations, package specs, quotes/paths, separators and allowed installs. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test, npm run docstring and npm run changelog:check PASS. Linked guard/workflow contracts passed through pm test --run --only-last --progress: 58 pass, 0 fail/cancel/skip/todo. Full-suite certification remains with CI; the review thread remains untouched."
  "2026-11-17T01:51:21.324Z",codex-sol,"Review round AA: pulled and verified the open PR head. Source inspection confirms the reported guard gaps. Replace shell tokenization with conservative logical-line matching and step-only script extraction, with intended false positives and regression fixtures."
  "2026-11-17T01:58:36.115Z",codex-sol,Typecheck and test compilation passed. This package has no lint script; attempting its installed pm-ops ESLint export failed because the optional @babel/eslint-parser peer is absent. No dependencies added. Running the remaining configured gates separately; lint remains unavailable in this package.
  "2026-11-17T02:02:14.278Z",codex-sol,"All four scoped threads verified valid against the original source: PRRT_kwDOUMUq1864GMbu, PRRT_kwDOUMUq1864LIvy, PRRT_kwDOUMUq1864LIv5, PRRT_kwDOUMUq1864LIwE. Direct reproduction returned zero findings for the seven unsafe shell cases and the named-step/folded workflows. Replaced tokenization with conservative logical-line matching; the dependency-free adapter extracts only step run scalars and fails closed on unsupported layouts. Final guard plus release-approval suite: 59 passed; separate release-workflow suite: 15 passed. Typecheck, test compilation and changelog:check passed. No duplication script is configured. Changed-file lint passed using the already installed shared pm-ops policy; AA_ESLINT_MODULE selects its complete installed module because this package has no lint script and lacks the optional local parser peer. No dependencies added. No findings refused. Full-suite certification remains with CI."
  "2026-11-17T03:33:06.442Z",pi-claude,"Round AF follow-up on the fail-closed guard, from review threads pm-ado PRRT_kwDOUMUq1864PGRG and PRRT_kwDOUMUq1864P73_ (with the identical pm-lint threads PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64QBn2, PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64QBn6 and PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64QBn7 replicated in this repository). All three findings were reproduced against the guard first: the prefix bootstrap followed by '&& npm install -g npm@11.19.0', 'npm install -gpld npm@11.19.0' and step env NPM_CONFIG_GLOBAL=true were all accepted by the previous code.\n\n1. Segment-scoped prefix exception: run scripts now split into command segments at unquoted ;, &, | and newlines. The scanner tracks quote state across lines and $( … ) substitutions (which nest a fresh quoting context even inside double quotes), skips comments and here-document bodies, and any script that cannot be delimited with confidence (unbalanced quote or substitution) fails closed as 'undelimitable command line'. The job-local prefix exception now only covers the segment carrying it; rejected fixtures add 'npm install --prefix \"$RUNNER_TEMP/npm-11.19.0\" npm@11.19.0 && npm install -g npm@11.19.0' and 'npm install --prefix \"$RUNNER_TEMP/npm-local\" npm@11.19.0; npm install -g npm@11.19.0'. The approved bootstrap fixtures stay accepted.\n2. Combined short flags: any single-dash letter cluster containing g now marks global (rejected: 'npm install -gpld npm@11.19.0', 'npm install -dg npm@11.19.0'); 'npm install -D pnpm' and 'npm install -gpld pnpm' stay accepted.\n3. Workflow, job and step env compose for each step run, the step scope taking precedence; npm reads npm_config_* keys case-insensitively. npm_config_global set to anything other than false/0/empty, npm_config_location=global, a ${{ … }} expression value, or an unreadable env scope makes every npm install in that run global unless its own segment carries a job-local prefix. Fixtures cover step env flow mapping, job env flow and block styles, workflow env, expression values, location=global, step-override (job \"true\" + step \"false\" accepted) and accepted \"false\"/\"0\"/\"\" values.\n\nGates: guard suite 63 passed; release-approval and release-workflow suites 20 passed; typecheck, test build, docstring gate and changelog:check passed; changed-file lint passed with the shared installed pm-ops policy (this package configures no lint or duplication script). Every workflow in the repository still scans clean. Full-suite certification remains with CI."
  "2026-11-17T05:22:27.387Z",codex-sol,"Round AH: implement conservative run-wide global configuration and markers, install-family aliases, redirect-safe prefix segmentation, and comment-free effective prefix exemptions. Preserve all existing rejected fixtures and approved bootstrap workflows; verify required package gates before releasing the claim. No review-thread mutations."
  "2026-11-17T05:32:10.865Z",codex-sol,"Round AH verification: 118 tests passed with zero failures, cancellations or skips (103 guard fixtures plus release-workflow contracts). npm run build, npm run build:test, npm run typecheck, npm run docstring, npm run changelog:check and git diff --check passed. No lint or duplication scripts exist. The same run-wide configuration and markers, installing aliases, redirect preservation and effective prefix exemption fixes are applied as in the companion PRs. All earlier rejected fixtures and approved bootstrap workflows are retained. Shared shell-guard logic matches all four copies; the existing dependency-free YAML extractor is preserved. Protected item dates are unchanged. Exact-head CI remains pending; no review-thread actions, publishing or merges."
  "2026-11-17T07:32:59.563Z",pi-guard-1117aj,"Round AJ: replaced the guard's per-segment shell parser with a line-based fail-closed rule (no shell parsing; logical lines only, comments and here-document text scanned like any other text). Install family now covers update/up/upgrade/udpate; markers cover single-dash g clusters, any global-containing token, -L with any value, and >=2-letter prefixes of global/location; run-wide npm config set/set signals; npm operands cover npm substrings (tarball URLs, x@npm:npm) and computed tokens; exemptions are exact approved bootstrap lines only; GITHUB_ENV npm_config_* writes and global/location npmrc writes reject the writing step. Narrowed the run-wide config signal to a set token because the release workflow's read-only 'npm config get globalconfig' tripped it; reworded one run comment that read like the forbidden command."
  "2026-11-17T08:23:12.141Z",codex-sol,"Round AM verified against unchanged guard: punctuation and comment-continuation bypasses, operandless global installs, persistent npm config setters, and spaced YAML env keys reproduce. Quoted command words already reject; add explicit regression coverage. Keep line-based checks and exact raw-line bootstrap matching. Unresolved review threads: PRRT_kwDOUMUq1864UpCw, PRRT_kwDOUMUq1864VA7b, PRRT_kwDOUMUq1864VA7e. Delegated npx finding is already rejected by Round AJ; preserve its rejected fixture. Run targeted gates directly; never execute linked PM tests. Preserve the existing test-session isolation import in the pm-vcs fixture."
  "2026-11-17T08:29:06.709Z",codex-sol,"Round AM targeted verification: 174 tests passed with zero failures, cancellations or skips. node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/global-npm-guard.test.ts test/release-workflow.test.ts test/release-approval.test.ts => PASS; npm run typecheck => PASS; npm run changelog:check => PASS. Scripts absent: lint, duplicates. All real workflows pass the guard; no bootstrap trailing comment was found. Guard source md5 d7ec9edd85b0c9fbe3d5a9f0e4d8d9e2 is identical across five packages. Fixture bodies match, retaining the required pm-vcs session-isolation import. Protected root item dates are unchanged; rejected fixtures are preserved. Same-class config persistence and spaced YAML env-key fixes from PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64VRGg, PRRT_kwDOToJT7M64U3xi and PRRT_kwDOVHTnEc64VRGj were applied to every copy. Full-suite certification remains with CI. Releasing this claim without closing the item."
